  "notes": "Sorcerer L-2 gameplay with direct public switch writes only (keyboard handling and the driver's simulator stay off). Two balls rest on ball ramp switches 29 and 30 and attract mode is observed for 40 s; a coin and the credit button start a game and the ROM serves a ball with the ramp eject (2) into the shooter lane (31). Jet and kicker switches show PinMAME's switch-driven special solenoids, 82 and 84 show the flipper column copy into 44 and the synthetic 45-48, the 3-bank is completed and reset (4), a first ramp shot locks a ball on 37 and the ROM serves the second ball (2), a second ball resting on the ramp switch (38) makes the ROM eject the lock (3), both balls drain through the outhole (28, kicked by 1) and the ROM serves ball 2, and three playfield-tilt closures (45) end that ball. Run from an NVRAM initialized by one prior empty-NVRAM power-up.",
  "watch_switches": [
    -7,
    -6,
    44
  ],
